Beryllium: beryllium://sandbox shows what the kernel says about every process

Purpose: plan/18 section 2 (feature matrix S-STA-02, S-STA-03). The page
  existed and was empty. The port registers Chromium's sandbox page on BSD,
  but the code that fills it is compiled for Linux and ChromeOS only, and
  the page's script asks for values nobody set.
  - chrome/browser/ui/webui/sandbox/sandbox_internals_ui.cc: on FreeBSD the
    page is written in the browser each time it is asked for, through the
    data source's request filter, as plain text in a fixed shape. It runs
    no script and uses none of Chromium's page resources. It has:
      - one line for the browser, each renderer and each other child
        process: its kind, its pid, capability mode by the kernel (yes, no
        or unknown, from KernelSaysCapabilityMode), whether the browser
        asked it to lock down, and for those whether the browser's check at
        connect passed;
      - a summary that counts, and makes no judgement: renderers in
        capability mode N of M, other child processes K of L, the browser
        process not confined;
      - whether the lockdown feature is on, how many renderers the kernel
        attested this session and how many the browser ended, whether the
        receive-side limits are on, whether --no-sandbox is in effect, and
        the kernel's name and release.
  Nothing on the page is a process's own report. Capability mode is read
    from the kernel when the page is loaded; reloading reads it again.
  Why not Chromium's page with a FreeBSD branch in its script: that needs
    changes to a TypeScript resource and its build rules, which this tree
    has never compiled a change to. One C++ file is the smaller risk for a
    build that takes hours, and plain lines are what the test suite needs.
Stage: 4 (Beryllium series). Depends on
  beryllium-kernel-attested-renderer.patch (the kernel's answer, the
  records) and beryllium-receive-limits-switch.patch (the feature it
  reports).
Refreshed against: Chromium 156.0.8078.79, Helium 0.20.3 (2f81b9ca),
  FreeBSD ports 6ad3e0c8, using freebsd/tools/patch-workbench. First
  built in 0.20.3.21 (released 16 November 2026): every line agrees with
  procstat -s, except that a renderer still starting is listed as not
  confined for a moment (the page's own, each time it opens in a new tab).
Test: freebsd/tests/browser/tests/test_50_sandbox.py
  test_sandbox_page_matches_the_kernel reads the page and compares the
  capability mode on every line with procstat -s for that pid, with the
  lockdown on and off; freebsd/tools/tests/test_sandbox_status.py tests the
  page's parser on a copy of the text this patch writes.
security-review: required (sandbox reporting)

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/sandbox/sandbox_internals_ui.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/sandbox/sandbox_internals_ui.cc
@@ -31,8 +31,171 @@
 #include "sandbox/policy/sandbox.h"
 #endif
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_FREEBSD)
+#include <unistd.h>
+
+#include "base/command_line.h"
+#include "base/feature_list.h"
+#include "base/functional/bind.h"
+#include "base/memory/ref_counted_memory.h"
+#include "base/memory/scoped_refptr.h"
+#include "base/posix/capsicum_rights.h"
+#include "base/process/process.h"
+#include "base/strings/escape.h"
+#include "base/strings/string_number_conversions.h"
+#include "base/strings/utf_string_conversions.h"
+#include "base/system/sys_info.h"
+#include "content/public/browser/browser_child_process_host_iterator.h"
+#include "content/public/browser/child_process_data.h"
+#include "content/public/browser/render_process_host.h"
+#include "content/public/common/process_type.h"
+#endif
+
 namespace {
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_FREEBSD)
+// Beryllium (plan/18 section 2; feature matrix S-STA-02, S-STA-03): the
+// page is written here, in the browser, each time it is asked for. Every
+// value comes from the kernel (kern.proc.pid) or from the browser's own
+// records at that moment; nothing on it is a child's own report, and the
+// page runs no script. Its lines are plain text in a fixed shape, so that
+// the test suite can compare each one with procstat.
+const char* BerylliumAnswer(base::freebsd::KernelAnswer answer) {
+  switch (answer) {
+    case base::freebsd::KernelAnswer::kYes:
+      return "yes";
+    case base::freebsd::KernelAnswer::kNo:
+      return "no";
+    case base::freebsd::KernelAnswer::kUnknown:
+      return "unknown";
+  }
+  return "unknown";
+}
+
+std::string BerylliumSandboxStatusHtml() {
+  std::string rows;
+  int renderers = 0;
+  int renderers_confined = 0;
+  int others = 0;
+  int others_confined = 0;
+
+  // One line a process: kind, pid, the kernel's answer, whether the browser
+  // asked it to lock down, whether the browser's check at connect passed.
+  const auto add_row = [&rows](const std::string& kind, base::ProcessId pid,
+                               base::freebsd::KernelAnswer answer,
+                               const char* requested, const char* attested) {
+    rows += "process: " + base::EscapeForHTML(kind) +
+            " | pid: " + base::NumberToString(pid) +
+            " | capability mode by the kernel: " + BerylliumAnswer(answer) +
+            " | lockdown requested: " + requested +
+            " | attested at connect: " + attested + "\n";
+  };
+
+  add_row("browser", getpid(),
+          base::freebsd::KernelSaysCapabilityMode(getpid()), "no",
+          "not applicable");
+
+  for (auto it = content::RenderProcessHost::AllHostsIterator(); !it.IsAtEnd();
+       it.Advance()) {
+    const base::Process& process = it.GetCurrentValue()->GetProcess();
+    if (!process.IsValid() || process.is_current()) {
+      continue;
+    }
+    const base::ProcessId pid = process.Pid();
+    const base::freebsd::KernelAnswer answer =
+        base::freebsd::KernelSaysCapabilityMode(pid);
+    const bool requested = base::freebsd::IsConfinedPeer(pid);
+    ++renderers;
+    if (answer == base::freebsd::KernelAnswer::kYes) {
+      ++renderers_confined;
+    }
+    add_row("renderer", pid, answer, requested ? "yes" : "no",
+            !requested ? "not applicable"
+                       : base::freebsd::WasAttested(pid) ? "yes" : "no");
+  }
+
+  for (content::BrowserChildProcessHostIterator it; !it.Done(); ++it) {
+    const base::Process& process = it.GetProcess();
+    if (!process.IsValid() || process.is_current()) {
+      continue;
+    }
+    const content::ChildProcessData& data = it.GetData();
+    std::string kind = content::GetProcessTypeNameInEnglish(data.process_type);
+    if (!data.metrics_name.empty()) {
+      kind += " (" + data.metrics_name + ")";
+    } else if (!data.name.empty()) {
+      kind += " (" + base::UTF16ToUTF8(data.name) + ")";
+    }
+    const base::ProcessId pid = process.Pid();
+    const base::freebsd::KernelAnswer answer =
+        base::freebsd::KernelSaysCapabilityMode(pid);
+    ++others;
+    if (answer == base::freebsd::KernelAnswer::kYes) {
+      ++others_confined;
+    }
+    add_row(kind, pid, answer, "no", "not applicable");
+  }
+
+  const base::CommandLine& command_line =
+      *base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess();
+  const bool lockdown =
+      base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(base::freebsd::kBerylliumCapsicumRenderer);
+  const bool receive_limits = base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(
+      base::freebsd::kBerylliumReceiveSideLimits);
+  const bool no_sandbox = command_line.HasSwitch("no-sandbox");
+
+  std::string page =
+      "<!doctype html>\n<html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">"
+      "<title>Sandbox status</title></head><body><pre>\n"
+      "Beryllium sandbox status\n\n"
+      "Every value below was read in the browser when this page was loaded:\n"
+      "capability mode from the kernel (kern.proc.pid, what procstat -s\n"
+      "prints as C), the rest from the browser's own records. Nothing here\n"
+      "is a process's own report. Reload the page to read again.\n\n";
+  page += "summary: renderers in capability mode: " +
+          base::NumberToString(renderers_confined) + " of " +
+          base::NumberToString(renderers) +
+          "; other child processes in capability mode: " +
+          base::NumberToString(others_confined) + " of " +
+          base::NumberToString(others) +
+          "; the browser process is not confined\n\n";
+  page += rows;
+  page += "\nrenderer lockdown (BerylliumCapsicumRenderer): ";
+  page += lockdown ? "on" : "off";
+  page += "\nrenderers attested by the kernel at connect, this session: " +
+          base::NumberToString(base::freebsd::AttestedTotal());
+  page += "\nrenderers ended because the kernel did not attest them, this "
+          "session: " +
+          base::NumberToString(base::freebsd::EndedUnattestedTotal());
+  page += "\nreceive-side limits (BerylliumReceiveSideLimits): ";
+  page += receive_limits ? "on" : "off, a test configuration";
+  page += "\nswitches in effect that weaken a sandbox: ";
+  page += no_sandbox ? "--no-sandbox" : "none";
+  page += "\nkernel: " +
+          base::EscapeForHTML(base::SysInfo::OperatingSystemName() + " " +
+                              base::SysInfo::OperatingSystemVersion());
+  page += "\n\nWith the lockdown off, no process is confined, and a page that\n"
+          "takes over a renderer has the access you have. With it on, the\n"
+          "renderers are confined and the browser, GPU, network and storage\n"
+          "processes are not. man beryllium-sandbox says what that means.\n"
+          "</pre></body></html>\n";
+  return page;
+}
+
+bool BerylliumShouldHandleRequest(const std::string& path) {
+  // The page itself, with or without a query. The other paths are the
+  // resources of Chromium's page, which this one does not use.
+  return path.empty() || path[0] == '?' || path[0] == '#';
+}
+
+void BerylliumHandleRequest(
+    const std::string& path,
+    content::WebUIDataSource::GotDataCallback callback) {
+  std::move(callback).Run(base::MakeRefCounted<base::RefCountedString>(
+      BerylliumSandboxStatusHtml()));
+}
+#endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_FREEBSD)
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
 static void SetSandboxStatusData(content::WebUIDataSource* source) {
   // Get expected sandboxing status of renderers.
@@ -81,6 +244,11 @@
   SetSandboxStatusData(source);
   source->UseStringsJs();
 #endif
+
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_FREEBSD)
+  source->SetRequestFilter(base::BindRepeating(&BerylliumShouldHandleRequest),
+                           base::BindRepeating(&BerylliumHandleRequest));
+#endif
 }
 
 }  // namespace
